  "limitations": [
    "The target was constructed predominantly from map taxonomy/name/review rules. 522/548 positive records have category toy_store. This count describes the mapped input category, not independent ground truth.",
    "Only 41 of 548 positive labels and one comparator label carry official_exact_address verification. Remaining 507 positives are explicitly unverified proxies. These purposive/development corrections are not an independent holdout and cannot estimate population label precision or recall.",
    "The model allowlist excludes own category, name, brand and all target-supply counts/distances. Thus the main analysis can examine contextual associations with mapped specialist status, but cannot infer profitability, unmet purchase demand, closure success or commercial outcome.",
    "Small marginal Pearson/Spearman coefficients do not prove zero predictive signal: nonlinear patterns/interactions may differ. They also do not establish useful out-of-area prediction. No model was trained in this audit.",
    "A 0.9365% positive class makes overall accuracy misleading; the majority-class fraction is recorded descriptively, not evaluated as a trained model.",
    "The denominator is retained source-qualified mapped retail sites after cleaning/complete-case selection. It is neither all California retailers nor all eligible available premises; source coverage and taxonomy differ by county/category.",
    "Many records share the same Census tract values, and neighboring sites share commercial context. The number of rows exceeds the number of independent demographic/spatial units. County/tract counts are provided to show support; no ordinary row-level p-values are claimed.",
    "No positive label in a county/tract means no retained mapped positive observation, not proven absence of specialist stores. Small county denominators/positive counts prevent precise geographic conclusions.",
    "ACS features describe the pooled 2020-2024 resident population, not store customers/visits; map input is an October 2026 snapshot. Income endpoint encoding and original ACS sampling uncertainty remain.",
    "A perceived underserved area requires additional demand/supply validation, coverage assessment and site constraints. Descriptive correlation or a mapped-label model alone cannot prove it."
  ],
